---
title: Design Tokens Overview
---

All visual styles for the Vonage Video React App are driven by a single file at the project root: **`theme.json`**. This is the one place you need to go to control colors, typography, and shape.

## Where It Lives

{% filetree %}

- theme.json ← All theme configuration goes here
- backend/
- frontend/
- libs/

{% /filetree %}

## File Structure

`theme.json` has four top-level sections:

```json
{
  "metadata": { },
  "colors": {
    "light": { },
    "dark": { }
  },
  "borderRadius": {
    "medium": 8
  },
  "typography": {
    "font-family": "Inter, sans-serif, system-ui, ui-sans-serif, Marker Felt, Trebuchet MS",
    "desktop": { },
    "mobile": { }
  }
}
```

- **`metadata`** — Identifies the theme document and schema version.
- **`colors.light` / `colors.dark`** — Separate color palettes for each mode. Both modes use the same set of kebab-case semantic token keys.
- **Typography tokens** — Sit under `typography` and apply to both modes. Includes `font-family` and separate `desktop` and `mobile` trees.
- **Shape tokens** — Sit under `borderRadius`. Six numeric values control the roundness of buttons, cards, and dialogs.

### Key color tokens

| Token           | Role                                  |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| `primary`       | Brand accent — buttons, active states |
| `primary-hover`  | Hover state of the primary color      |
| `surface`       | Card and panel backgrounds            |
| `background`    | Page background                       |
| `text-primary`   | Primary text color                    |
| `text-secondary` | Secondary / subdued text              |
| `error`         | Destructive actions and error states  |
| `success`       | Confirmation and success states       |

## Opening the File

The file is already open in your editor. You can also open it from the terminal:

```sh
code theme.json
```

Now let's start by customizing the color palette.
